 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "For curves it can be deduced from [sk-thm-picard-pn] and\nthe adjunction of the canonical sheaf with the Cartier picture of\ndivisors (the residue sequence). The analogue for a smooth proper\n$X$ of any dimension holds as well. Local freeness cannot be\ndropped in this form: for the skyscraper $\\cF=\\kappa(x)$ at a closed\npoint of $\\mathbf P^1$ one has $H^0(\\cF)^\\vee\\neq0$ but\n$\\cF^\\vee=\\mathcal Hom(\\kappa(x),\\cO)=0$; for coherent $\\cF$ the right\nside must be replaced by $\\operatorname{Ext}^{n-q}(\\cF,\\omega_X)$.",
   "uses": [
    "sk-thm-picard-pn"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
